PROPOSAL: product-direction decision for the maintainer; do not implement without a go-ahead.

Evidence: Docker::API's after_build uses the built dist (no .git) as build context (Dist/Zilla/Plugin/Docker/API.pm:336); Dockerfile:27 runs `dzil build` inside it, which fails ("fatal: not a git repository", exit 128, simulated). A manual `docker build .` from the checkout gets past dzil, but then the tarball's tests fail (dist-tests card). Not run as a real docker build (base image not pulled). Related waste: Dockerfile:20 `cpanm --installdeps --cpanfile cpanfile` without a target installs nothing (no cached dependency layer); :26 installs Dist::Zilla + bundle into the system site_perl that :44 copies into the runtime stage; :17 reinstalls cpanm; :33-34 install zlib1g-dev/libssl3 that nothing needs; :55 EXPOSE 8080 on a stdio server; the :47 comment "Copy wiki root" is wrong.
Why a proposal: it changes how the k7 image is built.
Options: (a) the Dockerfile installs the already-built dist from its context (`cpanm --installdeps . && cpanm .`), no dzil inside the image; manual builds go through `dzil build`; (b) keep dzil in the image, build only by hand from the checkout, drop the Docker::API wiring (reverses k7); (c) support both with a stage that checks for Makefile.PL.
Recommendation: (a), together with the layer clean-up.

2026-10-26 19:51 Decision (coordinator, on the maintainer's order to work the board off): option (a) with the layer clean-up: the image installs the built dist (cpanm --installdeps . as a cached layer, then cpanm .), no dzil in the image. Branch docker.
